From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Ferralis <ferralis@generalflash.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:27:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: configurable input limits, bottom-face features,
 training goals from a goals file

- Model input limits as S1Config options: max_nodes (feature-tree objects encoded, upstream
  40), max_goal (goal intents, 24), max_ord / max_pos (ordinal and position tables, 32 / 128),
  newest_nodes (a longer tree keeps the Body and the newest objects instead of the oldest;
  ordinals are counted over the whole tree). Defaults are upstream's, so existing checkpoints
  load and featurize exactly as before; non-default limits are featurization options (and
  part of the data cache name). train_sft: --heads, --max-nodes, --max-goal, --max-ord,
  --max-pos, --newest-nodes. Token positions and ordinals are int16.
- Features on the bottom face (Face-Z) in the side and mixed families.
- ext/goalsfile.py: TAIGA_GOALS_FILE / TAIGA_GOALS_FRACTION draw that share of the training
  goals from goals files (e.g. verified DeepCAD designs), by length (1 intent: level 1, 2-3:
  level 2, 4+: level 3, no upper limit); held-out compositions are dropped; evaluation splits
  are unaffected.
